---
// Privacy policy in English, a convenience translation of the German Datenschutzerklärung
// (src/pages/de/datenschutz.astro), which is the legally binding version. Same facts, same checks:
// GitHub Pages hosting, self hosted fonts, no cookies or tracking of its own, the consent record and
// the explicit language choice (locale-explicit) in localStorage, the cal.com embed on the home and
// booking pages only after consent (incl. Cloudflare __cf_bm cookie and Sentry), plain external
// links. Change both pages together, whenever a third party service or a storage key is added or
// removed. While the demo calendar is configured (CAL_IS_DEMO), the booking section names the holder
// of the demo account as recipient.
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { site, company, contact, contentUpdated, type NavItem } from '../config/site';
import { CAL_IS_DEMO, CAL_DEMO_ACCOUNT_HOLDER } from '../config/booking';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { CONSENT_STORAGE_KEY } from '../config/consent';
import { anchor, t } from '../i18n';

const consentId = anchor('consent', 'en');
const bookingId = anchor('booking-calendar', 'en');

const title = `Privacy policy | ${site.name}`;
const description = `Privacy policy of ${site.domain}: hosting on GitHub Pages, online booking via cal.com, consent, contact, your rights. No cookies of our own, no tracking.`;
const breadcrumbs: NavItem[] = [{ label: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' }];

const toc: NavItem[] = [
  { label: 'Controller', href: '#controller' },
  { label: 'Hosting on GitHub Pages', href: '#hosting' },
  { label: 'Fonts, cookies and tracking', href: '#cookies' },
  { label: 'Consent and cookie settings', href: `#${consentId}` },
  { label: 'Online booking via cal.com', href: `#${bookingId}` },
  { label: 'Contact by email and telephone', href: '#contact' },
  { label: 'Links to other services', href: '#links' },
  { label: 'Your rights', href: '#rights' },
  { label: 'Complaint to the supervisory authority', href: '#complaint' },
];

const external = { target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer' };
---

<ArticleLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  heading="Privacy policy"
  lead="These pages work without cookies of their own, without analytics and without advertising services. Besides the hosting on GitHub Pages, one further service only comes into play with your consent: the calendar for online booking."
  label="Legal"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  updated={contentUpdated}
  asideFirst
>
  <p>
    This English text is a convenience translation. The legally binding version is the German
    <a href={url('/de/datenschutz/')} hreflang="de">Datenschutzerklärung</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="controller">Controller</h2>
  <p>The controller responsible for the processing of personal data on this website is:</p>
  <p>
    {company.name}<br />
    {company.street}<br />
    {contact.postalCode} {contact.city}<br />
    {t('en').site.country}<br />
    Represented by the managing director {company.managingDirector}
  </p>
  <p>
    Telephone: <a href={contact.phone.href}>{contact.phone.display}</a><br />
    Email: <a class="break-all" href={contact.email.href}>{contact.email.display}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    No data protection officer has been appointed. Please send any questions about data protection to the contact
    details above.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosting">Hosting on GitHub Pages</h2>
  <p>
    This website is served via GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco,
    CA 94107, USA. When you open a page, your browser sends technically necessary data to the servers of GitHub. This
    includes your IP address, the date and time of the request, the address requested, the page visited before
    (referrer) and details of your browser and operating system.
  </p>
  <p>
    According to GitHub, it stores the IP addresses of visitors to GitHub Pages for security purposes. We have no
    access to these logs and do not evaluate them. GitHub determines how long it keeps them.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). Our legitimate interest lies in
    providing the website securely and reliably.
  </p>
  <p>
    This involves a transfer of data to the USA. GitHub is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, so the
    transfer is covered by the adequacy decision of the European Commission under Art. 45 GDPR. In addition, GitHub
    relies on the standard contractual clauses of the European Commission. Details are set out in the
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" {...external}
      >privacy statement of GitHub<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new window)</span></a
    >.
  </p>
  <p>All pages are transmitted encrypted via HTTPS.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Fonts, cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    The fonts of this website are stored on the same server as the website itself. Loading them sends no data to font
    providers such as Google Fonts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our own pages set no cookies. In your browser storage they keep at most two entries: your answer to the question
    about consent and, if you close the language notice or switch the language, that choice. Both are described in
    the next section. We use no analytics or audience measurement, no advertising services and no social media
    plugins. One third-party service, the calendar of cal.com, only loads with your consent.
  </p>

  <h2 id={consentId}>Consent and cookie settings</h2>
  <p>
    On your first visit we ask whether the cal.com booking calendar may load. Rejecting is as easy as accepting, and
    without consent the website works in full. Before you consent, nothing is loaded from cal.com and no connection to
    cal.com is made. Instead of the calendar you see a placeholder, from which you can load the calendar with your
    consent or arrange the appointment by telephone or email.
  </p>
  <p>
    We store your answer in your browser so that we do not ask again on every page. Your browser also remembers when
    you close the notice about the other language version or switch the language yourself:
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Entry</th>
          <th scope="col">Location</th>
          <th scope="col">Written</th>
          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
          <th scope="col">Storage period</th>
          <th scope="col">Consent</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{CONSENT_STORAGE_KEY}</th>
          <td>localStorage of this website</td>
          <td>when you make a choice in the notice or in the cookie settings</td>
          <td>
            Stores your choice: the version of the notice, the time and whether the calendar may load. No identifier,
            read only by this website.
          </td>
          <td>until you change your choice or clear your browser storage</td>
          <td>not required, strictly necessary (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">locale-explicit</th>
          <td>localStorage of this website</td>
          <td>when you close the language notice or choose the language with the language switch</td>
          <td>Keeps the notice about the other language version from showing again. Value 1, no identifier, read only by this website.</td>
          <td>until you clear your browser storage</td>
          <td>not required, strictly necessary (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    TDDDG stands for the German Telecommunications Digital Services Data Protection Act
    (Telekommunikation-Digitale-Dienste-Datenschutz-Gesetz), which governs storing and reading information on your
    device. The legal basis for processing these entries is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our legitimate interest lies in
    respecting your decisions and being able to demonstrate your consent decision (Art. 7(1) GDPR). The entries never
    leave your browser. If the notice changes in substance, we ask again.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can withdraw or change your consent at any time with effect for the future, via the Cookie settings link at the
    bottom of every page or
    <a href={url(`/privacy/#${consentId}`)} data-consent-open aria-haspopup="dialog">right here</a>. If the calendar has
    already loaded, the page reloads after the withdrawal so that it is removed. The lawfulness of processing before
    the withdrawal remains unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2 id={bookingId}>Online booking via cal.com</h2>
  <p>
    To book the free first consultation, we embed a calendar of the cal.com service. The provider is Cal.com, Inc.,
    2261 Market Street #4382, San Francisco, CA 94114, USA.
  </p>
  <h3>When the calendar loads</h3>
  <p>
    The calendar is on the <a href={url(`/#${anchor('booking', 'en')}`)}>home page</a> and on the
    <a href={url('/booking/')}>booking page</a>. It only loads if you have consented, in the privacy notice, in the
    cookie settings or with the Load calendar and consent button in the booking section. Even then it does not load
    with the page, but only once the booking section comes into view. From that moment your browser retrieves content
    from cal.com servers. On all other pages nothing is loaded from cal.com.
  </p>
  <h3>Which data is processed</h3>
  <p>
    As soon as the calendar loads, cal.com receives technical data: your IP address, details of your browser and
    device, the address of the page in which the calendar is embedded, and the date and time. Cloudflare, a service
    provider used by cal.com, sets the cookie __cf_bm, which serves to fend off automated access (bots) and expires
    after 30 minutes of inactivity. The calendar also sends technical error reports to the Sentry service, which
    cal.com uses for error analysis.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you book an appointment, cal.com also processes the details you enter in the booking form, in particular your
    name, email address, the chosen time and your message. cal.com sends the booking confirmation by email.
  </p>
  {
    CAL_IS_DEMO ? (
      <p>
        At present, a demo calendar for the preview is embedded on this website. It sits in the cal.com account of the
        web developer of this website, {CAL_DEMO_ACCOUNT_HOLDER}, not in an account of {company.name}. Details from a
        booking therefore go to that account and not to us, and no appointment with {site.expert} results from it. For
        a real first consultation, please call or send an email. As soon as the calendar of {company.name} is embedded,
        this notice will be removed.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>We receive these details in order to hold the appointment with you.</p>
    )
  }
  <h3>Legal basis</h3>
  <p>
    Loading the calendar and the associated transfer to cal.com are based on your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). Where
    information is stored on or read from your device in the process, such as the cookie __cf_bm, the legal basis is
    likewise your consent (§ 25(1) TDDDG). Processing your details when you book serves to take steps prior to
    entering into a contract at your request (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).
  </p>
  <p>
    You can withdraw your consent at any time with effect for the future, via
    <a href={url(`/privacy/#${consentId}`)} data-consent-open aria-haspopup="dialog">Cookie settings</a>. After that the
    calendar no longer loads. Cookies that cal.com has set on its own domain expire (__cf_bm after 30 minutes of
    inactivity) or can be deleted in your browser.
  </p>
  <h3>Transfer to the USA</h3>
  <p>
    Cal.com processes the data in the USA. Cal.com, Inc. is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework (as
    checked on 12 November 2026), so the transfer is based on the adequacy decision of the European Commission under
    Art. 45 GDPR. For transfers outside this framework, cal.com uses the standard contractual clauses of the European
    Commission. Details are set out in the
    <a href="https://cal.com/privacy" {...external}
      >privacy policy of cal.com<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new window)</span></a
    >.
  </p>
  <h3>Storage period and alternatives</h3>
  <p>
    {
      CAL_IS_DEMO ? (
        <>
          We do not receive booking data from the demo calendar. It is held in the cal.com account of{' '}
          {CAL_DEMO_ACCOUNT_HOLDER} and is stored and deleted under the rules of cal.com.
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          We delete booking data as soon as it is no longer needed to hold and follow up the appointment, unless
          statutory retention obligations apply.
        </>
      )
    }{' '}
    If you do not consent or do not want to use cal.com, simply arrange your appointment by telephone on{' '}
    <a href={contact.phone.href}>{contact.phone.display}</a> or by email.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact by email and telephone</h2>
  <p>
    If you email or call us, we process your details, such as your name, contact details, your request and any photos
    or documents you send, in order to handle your enquiry. Where it concerns a report or a commission, the legal basis
    is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, with the legitimate interest of answering enquiries.
  </p>
  <p>
    The email mailbox is operated by the provider WEB.DE of 1&amp;1 Mail &amp; Media GmbH, Brauerstraße 48, 76135
    Karlsruhe, Germany. Your messages are therefore also stored on their servers.
  </p>
  <p>
    We delete your enquiry once it has been dealt with and no statutory retention obligations apply. Business letters
    and documents relating to commissions are kept for up to ten years under German commercial and tax law (§ 257 HGB,
    § 147 AO).
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">Links to other services</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages link to other providers, for example to Google Maps for directions to the office or to the cal.com
    booking page. Such links are plain references: data only goes to the provider once you click the link. From then
    on, the privacy policy of that provider applies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right at any time, towards {company.name}, to</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access to your stored data (Art. 15 GDPR),</li>
    <li>rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR),</li>
    <li>erasure of your data (Art. 17 GDPR),</li>
    <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR),</li>
    <li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR),</li>
    <li>withdraw consent you have given, with effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    An email to <a class="break-all" href={contact.email.href}>{contact.email.display}</a> is enough for any request.
  </p>
  <h3>Right to object</h3>
  <p>
    Where we process data on the basis of Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, you may object at any time on grounds relating to your
    particular situation (Art. 21 GDPR). We will then no longer process the data, unless there are compelling
    legitimate grounds for the processing or it serves the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims.
  </p>

  <h2 id="complaint">Complaint to the supervisory authority</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR). The authority
    responsible for {company.name} is:
  </p>
  <p>
    Der Hessische Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit (Hessian Commissioner for Data Protection and
    Freedom of Information)<br />
    Wilhelmstraße 7<br />
    65185 Wiesbaden<br />
    {t('en').site.country}<br />
    <a href="https://datenschutz.hessen.de" {...external}
      >datenschutz.hessen.de<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new window)</span></a
    >
  </p>

  <h2>Obligation to provide data and automated decisions</h2>
  <p>
    You are under no obligation to provide us with data. Without contact details, however, we cannot handle an enquiry
    or an appointment. No automated decision making, including profiling, takes place.
  </p>

  <nav slot="aside" aria-label="Contents of the privacy policy">
    <p class="label text-ink">On this page</p>
    <ul class="mt-2 grid">
      {
        toc.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <a class="link-ink inline-flex min-h-11 items-center" href={item.href}>{item.label}</a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </nav>
</ArticleLayout>
